      "html": "<h3>Do cleaning companies need COSHH assessments?</h3><p>Yes. Any employer whose people use hazardous substances must assess the risk. Cleaning products are among the commonest.</p><h3>Which cleaning products need one?</h3><p>Any that carry hazard labelling: bleach, descalers, oven and drain cleaners, disinfectants, degreasers and strippers. The safety data sheet and label say.</p><h3>Do cleaners have to be told?</h3><p>Yes. Regulation 12 asks for information, instruction and training on the substances, risks and controls.</p><h3>Does the client need a copy?</h3><p>Many clients ask for them. Quickler Records come back in your own Word form to share.</p><h3>Can I do several products at once?</h3><p>Yes. Do them one after another in one chat. Each is its own Record.</p>"
